1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:15,000
残酷な天使のように 少年よ 神話になれ

2
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:37,000
青い風が今 胸のドアを叩いても 私だけをただ見つめて 微笑んでるあなた

3
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:51,000
そっと触れるもの 求めることに夢中で 運命さえまだ知らない 痛い気な瞳

4
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:58,000
だけどいつか気づくでしょう その背中には

5
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:06,000
遥か未来 目指すための羽があること

6
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:14,000
残酷な天使の帝世 窓辺からやがて取り立つ

7
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:22,000
ほとばしる 熱いパッドスで 思い出を裏切るなら

8
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:29,000
この空を抱いて輝く 少年よ 神話になれ

9
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:37,700
NHK

10
00:01:37,700 --> 00:01:45,560
My last assignment, it's red, just like blood.

11
00:01:49,080 --> 00:01:50,880
Commander Fuyutsuki was abducted?

12
00:01:51,320 --> 00:01:53,640
Yes, it happened about two hours ago.

13
00:01:54,180 --> 00:01:56,400
The vice commander was last seen in the 8th district.

14
00:01:56,820 --> 00:01:58,080
That's inside this installation?

15
00:01:58,560 --> 00:02:00,600
What in the hell were you idiots in intelligence doing?

16
00:02:00,820 --> 00:02:03,480
Someone inside this organization must have been involved.

17
00:02:03,860 --> 00:02:06,080
We appreciate your cooperation in this.

18
00:02:06,080 --> 00:02:08,160
Someone who could outwit Section 2.

19
00:02:09,080 --> 00:02:10,260
Oh no, you don't think...

20
00:02:10,260 --> 00:02:11,220
My OG Kaji.

21
00:02:11,800 --> 00:02:14,140
He's the suspected mastermind behind this plot.

22
00:02:14,800 --> 00:02:16,360
So that's why you came for me.

23
00:02:16,780 --> 00:02:18,420
We believe that you can help us.

24
00:02:19,020 --> 00:02:23,760
As your colleagues, we regret the necessity of including the director of operations as a suspect.

25
00:02:24,120 --> 00:02:25,740
But that is the nature of our profession.

26
00:02:26,020 --> 00:02:30,060
And of course, considering my relationship with him, it's a natural precaution.

27
00:02:30,360 --> 00:02:32,800
Your cooperation would be appreciated.

28
00:02:33,420 --> 00:02:34,720
It's been a while.

29
00:02:34,720 --> 00:02:38,400
Are your invitations always so violent, Chairman Keel?

30
00:02:39,020 --> 00:02:43,220
There are a number of matters we need to discuss outside of Commander Akari's hearing.

31
00:02:43,680 --> 00:02:45,900
The nature of your procurement was necessary.

32
00:02:46,480 --> 00:02:47,800
You haven't changed at all.

33
00:02:48,340 --> 00:02:49,720
And how this affects me is inconsequential.

34
00:02:49,720 --> 00:02:53,460
The subject to be addressed has already become an active issue.

35
00:02:53,800 --> 00:02:57,140
Thus, these measures will inevitably please understand our situation.

36
00:02:57,260 --> 00:02:58,700
Oh, now this is surprising.

37
00:02:59,340 --> 00:03:01,440
Not the committee, but Sele itself.

38
00:03:01,600 --> 00:03:03,820
Creating a new god is not on our agenda.

39
00:03:04,180 --> 00:03:07,020
We hope that you will cooperate, Professor Fiyutski.

40
00:03:07,400 --> 00:03:08,540
Professor Fiyutski.

41
00:03:08,540 --> 00:03:13,460
Professor Fiyutski.

42
00:03:13,680 --> 00:03:14,080
Professor.

43
00:03:15,340 --> 00:03:16,540
Oh, hello, boys.

44
00:03:17,140 --> 00:03:19,420
Hey, why don't you come down and join us for a beer at the Riverwalk?

45
00:03:19,500 --> 00:03:19,840
What?

46
00:03:19,900 --> 00:03:20,220
Again?

47
00:03:20,500 --> 00:03:22,800
Ryoko and the other girls say they'll come if you'll come.

48
00:03:22,800 --> 00:03:26,540
And didn't the dean say you shouldn't be so unsociable?

49
00:03:27,140 --> 00:03:28,760
All right, you guys win.

50
00:03:29,720 --> 00:03:32,820
It's nice to have a chance to have a drink outside for a change.

51
00:03:33,240 --> 00:03:33,720
Yes.

52
00:03:34,180 --> 00:03:35,880
You know, you're a brilliant scientist.

53
00:03:36,540 --> 00:03:39,380
But you don't place enough value in your relationships with others.

54
00:03:39,580 --> 00:03:40,440
I'm sorry, sir.

55
00:03:40,840 --> 00:03:42,140
Somehow I doubt that.

56
00:03:42,440 --> 00:03:46,560
However, there's a young bioengineering student who's just written a very interesting paper.

57
00:03:47,200 --> 00:03:48,380
Her name is Ikari.

58
00:03:48,740 --> 00:03:50,520
Have you heard about her before?

59
00:03:50,780 --> 00:03:51,180
Ikari?

60
00:03:51,180 --> 00:03:52,300
No, sir.

61
00:03:52,460 --> 00:03:55,740
I've told her about your work, and she asked if she could meet you.

62
00:03:55,980 --> 00:03:59,840
She'll be calling you soon, and I'd like you to take her on as a research assistant.

63
00:04:00,140 --> 00:04:01,320
And her name is Ikari.

64
00:04:01,680 --> 00:04:02,420
I'll do it, sir.

65
00:04:04,200 --> 00:04:05,980
I read your paper last night.

66
00:04:06,160 --> 00:04:09,560
There are a few things I have questions about, but it's really, really very intriguing.

67
00:04:09,980 --> 00:04:11,520
Oh, thank you very much, sir.

68
00:04:11,560 --> 00:04:13,680
And your full name is Yui Ikari, right?

69
00:04:13,880 --> 00:04:14,560
Yes, sir.

70
00:04:14,860 --> 00:04:16,720
So, what are your career plans?

71
00:04:16,900 --> 00:04:20,860
Would you like to go into a corporate research or join a school's research facility?

72
00:04:21,180 --> 00:04:26,340
Well, I haven't really thought about it much, and in my case, there may be a third option to be considered.

73
00:04:27,340 --> 00:04:29,740
I'm thinking about getting married and having children.

74
00:04:30,220 --> 00:04:32,460
Of course, that's assuming that I meet the right person.

75
00:04:32,460 --> 00:04:41,800
By incorporating the S2 unit into itself, it has achieved its ultimate form, Evangelion Unit 1.

76
00:04:41,800 --> 00:04:43,860
A living god which we created.

77
00:04:44,080 --> 00:04:44,960
What blasphemy!

78
00:04:45,240 --> 00:04:47,820
The creation of a supreme being is unacceptable.

79
00:04:48,140 --> 00:04:50,280
Man must not create gods.

80
00:04:50,380 --> 00:04:52,260
No one should possess such power.

81
00:04:52,780 --> 00:04:54,400
Can we trust Gendo Ikari?

82
00:04:54,400 --> 00:04:56,560
Gendo Rokabungi?

83
00:04:56,880 --> 00:04:58,140
I've heard the name before.

84
00:04:58,920 --> 00:05:00,860
No, I've never met him.

85
00:05:01,180 --> 00:05:03,900
But he does seem to be at the core of a lot of rumors.

86
00:05:04,440 --> 00:05:06,240
Rather unsavory rumors of that.

87
00:05:07,760 --> 00:05:08,320
What?

88
00:05:08,860 --> 00:05:10,760
I was appointed as his advisor?

89
00:05:11,140 --> 00:05:12,300
Well, I'll come bail him out.

90
00:05:13,100 --> 00:05:15,600
I've been hearing some interesting things about you, Professor.

91
00:05:16,460 --> 00:05:18,900
I've been wanting to meet you for some time.

92
00:05:19,740 --> 00:05:23,320
Well, getting drunk and starting a fight isn't the best introduction.

93
00:05:23,460 --> 00:05:25,820
I didn't have a chance to say anything before they jumped me.

94
00:05:26,640 --> 00:05:28,200
I'm not used to being liked, Professor.

95
00:05:28,720 --> 00:05:30,460
But I'm quite familiar with hatred.

96
00:05:32,520 --> 00:05:34,600
Well, your problems are none of my concern.

97
00:05:35,040 --> 00:05:38,920
And you're exactly the kind of person that I expected Professor Fyutski to be.

98
00:05:40,100 --> 00:05:44,540
My first impression of him was that he was a rogue bull on a short tether.

99
00:05:44,540 --> 00:05:47,700
Back then, there were still seasons in this country.

100
00:05:48,220 --> 00:05:48,840
It was autumn.

101
00:05:49,700 --> 00:05:51,000
Are you serious?

102
00:05:51,240 --> 00:05:52,000
Yes, sir.

103
00:05:52,220 --> 00:05:54,060
I've been dating Gendo Rokabungi.

104
00:05:54,300 --> 00:05:54,920
A lot.

105
00:05:55,540 --> 00:05:58,020
When she told me that, I couldn't hide my shock.

106
00:05:59,840 --> 00:06:02,740
It's rather hard imagining you and him being together.

107
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:04,320
He's really very nice.

108
00:06:04,780 --> 00:06:07,560
It's just that nobody really knows him quite the way I do.

109
00:06:07,860 --> 00:06:09,280
You ought to try, sir.

110
00:06:09,540 --> 00:06:12,080
In this case, I think that ignorance might be bliss.

111
00:06:12,080 --> 00:06:15,260
Are you upset that I told him to list you as his counselor?

112
00:06:15,560 --> 00:06:20,760
Well, I'll admit that he's interesting, but I just don't like him.

113
00:06:21,540 --> 00:06:27,160
It was generally believed that the real object of Gendo's overtures to Yui was her obvious talent.

114
00:06:27,720 --> 00:06:32,340
That and the support of the secret organization that was arranging funding for her projects.

115
00:06:32,760 --> 00:06:34,720
That organization was called Sele.

116
00:06:34,720 --> 00:06:39,880
In the year 2000, the second impact occurred.

117
00:06:41,280 --> 00:06:45,720
The first year of the 21st century was, what can I say, uh...

118
00:06:45,720 --> 00:06:49,320
It was a time I still find hard to talk about.

119
00:06:52,580 --> 00:06:54,940
This used to be a continent of ice.

120
00:06:55,480 --> 00:06:56,740
The entire thing is gone.

121
00:06:57,580 --> 00:06:58,520
Professor Fiyutsuki!

122
00:06:59,680 --> 00:07:00,900
I don't believe it.

123
00:07:01,340 --> 00:07:02,100
You're alive.

124
00:07:02,100 --> 00:07:06,800
I had heard that you were with the Katsuragi research team when the disaster occurred.

125
00:07:07,060 --> 00:07:11,580
Fortunately, I returned to Japan one day before the incident happened.

126
00:07:11,860 --> 00:07:12,600
Is that so?

127
00:07:13,120 --> 00:07:14,780
Mr. Okabungi, you're a very...

128
00:07:14,780 --> 00:07:17,000
Excuse me, but I've changed my name.

129
00:07:19,100 --> 00:07:20,220
A postcard.

130
00:07:20,540 --> 00:07:21,480
Not a business card.

131
00:07:23,640 --> 00:07:24,080
Ikari?

132
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:26,040
Gendo Ikari?

133
00:07:26,280 --> 00:07:29,180
My wife has been asking me to send you this for a while now.

134
00:07:29,600 --> 00:07:31,420
She's still quite a fan of yours.

135
00:07:31,420 --> 00:07:33,040
Quite an honor, considering.

136
00:07:33,900 --> 00:07:35,280
So, how is Yui doing?

137
00:07:35,760 --> 00:07:37,240
Why isn't she on this expedition?

138
00:07:37,600 --> 00:07:39,480
Oh, Yui wanted to come as well.

139
00:07:39,860 --> 00:07:41,400
But we have a child to consider now.

140
00:07:43,080 --> 00:07:47,180
There are a lot of ugly rumors about this organization you work for.

141
00:07:47,940 --> 00:07:49,300
Sele, or whatever it's called.

142
00:07:49,780 --> 00:07:51,520
I don't like the way it bullies the committee.

143
00:07:51,720 --> 00:07:53,480
I'm afraid that it's necessary.

144
00:07:54,040 --> 00:07:57,220
An organization can't have too many scruples in this day and age.

145
00:07:57,280 --> 00:08:00,180
It may be true that Second Impact has changed a lot of things.

146
00:08:00,180 --> 00:08:04,060
But if this official investigation team had been composed solely of Sele personnel,

147
00:08:04,480 --> 00:08:05,420
there would have been trouble.

148
00:08:05,780 --> 00:08:08,240
Were the rest of us just invited for political convenience?

149
00:08:08,240 --> 00:08:15,400
I hate the darkness.

150
00:08:16,400 --> 00:08:19,060
All it does is bring back the most horrible memories.

151
00:08:19,900 --> 00:08:20,540
Who is she?

152
00:08:20,880 --> 00:08:22,800
The only survivor of the research team.

153
00:08:23,980 --> 00:08:26,180
Her name is Misato Katsuragi.

154
00:08:26,620 --> 00:08:27,140
Katsuragi?

155
00:08:27,520 --> 00:08:29,240
You mean Dr. Katsuragi's daughter?

156
00:08:29,240 --> 00:08:32,300
Yes, but she hasn't said a word in two years.

157
00:08:32,980 --> 00:08:33,860
How terrible.

158
00:08:34,660 --> 00:08:36,160
She saw hell firsthand.

159
00:08:36,840 --> 00:08:41,340
Her physical wounds could be healed, but repairing the damage to her mind will take time.

160
00:08:41,880 --> 00:08:42,440
Indeed.

161
00:08:42,440 --> 00:08:45,820
The results of our investigation aren't easy to analyze.

162
00:08:46,240 --> 00:08:49,300
This giant of light is but one of many mysteries.

163
00:08:49,940 --> 00:08:53,000
Later, the United Nations would make an official declaration.

164
00:08:53,500 --> 00:08:56,880
The Second Impact had been caused by a massive meteorite strike on Antarctica.

165
00:08:58,100 --> 00:09:02,160
As someone who knew what I knew, those announcements were obvious fabrications.

166
00:09:03,120 --> 00:09:05,980
Zele and a man named Kiel were behind the cover-up.

167
00:09:06,640 --> 00:09:12,520
It became my goal, my obsession to find the real answers, the truth that was being suppressed.

168
00:09:13,040 --> 00:09:16,560
Even if my former student, Yui, was involved as well.

169
00:09:16,960 --> 00:09:18,880
Why did you conceal the existence of the giant?

170
00:09:19,380 --> 00:09:21,680
You knew Second Impact was going to happen, didn't you?

171
00:09:22,060 --> 00:09:26,640
You could talk all you want to about how it was just luck that you returned one day before it occurred.

172
00:09:26,640 --> 00:09:31,020
But how do you explain the fact that you brought back all the expedition's records and findings?

173
00:09:31,020 --> 00:09:35,600
I know for a fact your personal files contain more than we recovered, Ikari.

174
00:09:37,940 --> 00:09:40,400
I'm surprised that these weren't destroyed.

175
00:09:40,900 --> 00:09:42,160
Sloppy housework.

176
00:09:42,840 --> 00:09:44,440
I've checked into your estate as well.

177
00:09:44,880 --> 00:09:47,020
Bringing up a child and educating him is expensive.

178
00:09:47,460 --> 00:09:50,420
But isn't it a bit much for a civil servant?

179
00:09:50,820 --> 00:09:52,900
Very impressive, Professor Fyutski.

180
00:09:53,340 --> 00:09:55,100
Perhaps you should be teaching economics?

181
00:09:55,480 --> 00:09:58,440
I'm going to go public with the real truth about you.

182
00:09:58,440 --> 00:10:00,860
Sail a second impact in the Dead Sea Scrolls.

183
00:10:01,200 --> 00:10:03,820
What you've done is completely inexcusable.

184
00:10:04,560 --> 00:10:05,280
As you wish.

185
00:10:05,940 --> 00:10:08,540
But first, there is something I'd like to show you.

186
00:10:10,860 --> 00:10:12,560
How far down are we going?

187
00:10:12,800 --> 00:10:13,840
Worried, Montresor?

188
00:10:14,300 --> 00:10:15,260
A little bit.

189
00:10:17,740 --> 00:10:18,840
Oh, my God!

190
00:10:18,840 --> 00:10:20,540
We didn't make this.

191
00:10:20,880 --> 00:10:25,520
Someone or something else excavated this cavity, although 89% of it was buried.

192
00:10:25,800 --> 00:10:28,420
Then this was originally a giant sphere?

193
00:10:28,640 --> 00:10:29,000
Yes.

194
00:10:29,320 --> 00:10:32,860
This geofront is what has been consuming the total resources of the human race.

195
00:10:39,020 --> 00:10:40,160
Professor Fyutski!

196
00:10:40,160 --> 00:10:43,740
Dr. Akagi, you're here too?

197
00:10:44,080 --> 00:10:44,440
Yes.

198
00:10:44,820 --> 00:10:49,920
This is the ideal place for advancing our research towards creating the ultimate biocomputer system.

199
00:10:50,480 --> 00:10:50,840
Hmm.

200
00:10:51,280 --> 00:10:53,160
I'm going to name them the Magi.

201
00:10:54,160 --> 00:10:54,860
The Magi?

202
00:10:55,320 --> 00:10:56,920
The three wise men of the East?

203
00:10:57,520 --> 00:10:59,220
Is this what you wanted to show me?

204
00:10:59,560 --> 00:10:59,860
No.

205
00:11:00,020 --> 00:11:00,940
It's over this way.

206
00:11:01,460 --> 00:11:02,720
Ritsuko, I'll be right back.

207
00:11:02,820 --> 00:11:03,040
Huh?

208
00:11:03,700 --> 00:11:03,980
Hmm.

209
00:11:03,980 --> 00:11:11,280
Is this a giant of light?

210
00:11:11,460 --> 00:11:11,700
No.

211
00:11:12,300 --> 00:11:15,300
In Gehern, we refer to the second impact giant as Adam.

212
00:11:15,520 --> 00:11:16,600
But this isn't the one.

213
00:11:17,620 --> 00:11:19,480
Then, what is this?

214
00:11:19,920 --> 00:11:22,440
This is what man has created from Adam.

215
00:11:22,920 --> 00:11:23,240
Ava.

216
00:11:23,480 --> 00:11:23,840
Ava?

217
00:11:24,380 --> 00:11:27,760
The operation to revive Adam is referred to as Project E.

218
00:11:27,760 --> 00:11:30,760
This is Ava Unit Zero, our system prototype.

219
00:11:31,200 --> 00:11:31,800
Prototype?

220
00:11:32,360 --> 00:11:33,460
Prototype of what?

221
00:11:33,460 --> 00:11:37,660
Fyutsuki, will you join us in creating a new genesis for mankind?

222
00:11:45,180 --> 00:11:46,260
Uh, ma'am?

223
00:11:47,020 --> 00:11:48,220
Oh, sorry.

224
00:11:48,460 --> 00:11:49,220
I zoned out.

225
00:11:49,820 --> 00:11:51,600
Let's proceed with Ray's repeat test.

226
00:11:52,420 --> 00:11:54,260
I haven't seen Major Katsuragi today.

227
00:11:54,720 --> 00:11:56,000
Uh, neither have I.

228
00:11:56,380 --> 00:11:56,680
Huh?

229
00:11:57,020 --> 00:11:57,580
Katsuragi?

230
00:11:58,080 --> 00:11:59,560
Yeah, Misaru Katsuragi.

231
00:11:59,720 --> 00:12:00,500
Pleased to meet ya!

232
00:12:01,200 --> 00:12:02,060
Dear Mother,

233
00:12:02,060 --> 00:12:05,720
I have just become acquainted with a girl named Katsuragi.

234
00:12:06,440 --> 00:12:10,360
Most people tend to keep their distance from me once they find out who I am, which forces

235
00:12:10,360 --> 00:12:12,560
me to remember how important your name is around here.

236
00:12:13,040 --> 00:12:14,320
But Misaru is different.

237
00:12:15,000 --> 00:12:16,440
She's very open and honest.

238
00:12:17,180 --> 00:12:17,940
Even with me.

239
00:12:18,260 --> 00:12:21,980
I also understand that she's the only survivor from the original research team.

240
00:12:22,340 --> 00:12:26,220
She used to be mute, but she talks almost constantly now, like she's trying to make up

241
00:12:26,220 --> 00:12:27,020
for lost time.

242
00:12:27,380 --> 00:12:31,300
Dear Ritsuko, I'm underground so much these days that I feel like a mole.

243
00:12:31,560 --> 00:12:35,360
And I'm getting royally sick and tired of living on the boxed lunches they provide here.

244
00:12:35,940 --> 00:12:37,040
That should improve, though.

245
00:12:37,380 --> 00:12:40,120
Up on the surface, they've started construction of Tokyo 3.

246
00:12:40,120 --> 00:12:44,600
Masato hasn't shown up at college for the last few days, and I finally forced her to tell

247
00:12:44,600 --> 00:12:45,100
me why.

248
00:12:45,520 --> 00:12:46,580
Talk about stupid.

249
00:12:46,960 --> 00:12:49,560
She spent the whole week having sex with her new boyfriend.

250
00:12:49,940 --> 00:12:50,880
A whole week!

251
00:12:51,080 --> 00:12:55,000
I think there's another side to her I haven't seen before, and it disturbs me.

252
00:12:55,420 --> 00:13:00,740
Well, she introduced me to him today, and he's handsome all right, but his sloppy grooming

253
00:13:00,740 --> 00:13:02,460
and attitude really bother me.

254
00:13:02,780 --> 00:13:05,100
You've always been a little boy, Shy Ritsuko, dear.

255
00:13:05,500 --> 00:13:08,520
I think it's because you only had a mother and no men in your life.

256
00:13:09,040 --> 00:13:12,060
And I'm afraid that I never reeled you in as often as I should have.

257
00:13:12,880 --> 00:13:16,740
I'm ashamed to admit it, but I've only acted like a mother when it suited my whims.

258
00:13:18,320 --> 00:13:19,440
Which wasn't often.

259
00:13:23,900 --> 00:13:27,140
The Strudel experiment will begin in five minutes.

260
00:13:27,160 --> 00:13:28,640
Why is there a child in here?

261
00:13:28,640 --> 00:13:31,100
That's Commander Akari's son.

262
00:13:31,740 --> 00:13:33,680
Akari, this isn't a daycare center.

263
00:13:34,260 --> 00:13:35,600
This is an important event.

264
00:13:36,260 --> 00:13:37,420
Sorry, Professor.

265
00:13:37,820 --> 00:13:39,500
I'm the one who brought Shinti here.

266
00:13:39,680 --> 00:13:42,640
But, Yui, this is your experiment today.

267
00:13:43,120 --> 00:13:44,540
That's why I brought him.

268
00:13:44,720 --> 00:13:46,980
I want to show him how bright the future will be.

269
00:13:47,480 --> 00:13:49,740
Those words would prove to be Yui's last.

270
00:13:50,940 --> 00:13:55,680
A freak accident wiped her from this existence, just as I had hoped it would.

271
00:13:55,680 --> 00:13:58,140
What a disgusting woman I am.

272
00:13:58,640 --> 00:14:04,460
Ritsuko, after that day, Commander Akari changed completely.

273
00:14:04,460 --> 00:14:07,680
Where have you been all week?

274
00:14:08,420 --> 00:14:09,780
I understand your grief.

275
00:14:10,300 --> 00:14:13,200
But you must know that your life no longer belongs to you alone.

276
00:14:13,880 --> 00:14:14,340
I know.

277
00:14:15,060 --> 00:14:17,860
Fyudski, as of today, we will begin the new project.

278
00:14:18,560 --> 00:14:20,960
I have already made the proposal to Chairman Keele.

279
00:14:20,960 --> 00:14:23,460
You mean it's approved?

280
00:14:23,620 --> 00:14:23,940
Yes.

281
00:14:24,440 --> 00:14:25,860
That which has never been achieved.

282
00:14:25,960 --> 00:14:27,760
The path to becoming one with God.

283
00:14:28,080 --> 00:14:29,800
The Human Instrumentality Project.

284
00:14:31,880 --> 00:14:36,060
Dear Mother, congratulations on the completion of your Magi Theorems.

285
00:14:36,060 --> 00:14:37,680
I have good news, too.

286
00:14:38,060 --> 00:14:40,580
It's been decided that I will officially join Gehearn.

287
00:14:40,840 --> 00:14:43,180
I'll start working on Project E next month.

288
00:14:43,180 --> 00:14:55,160
Dr. Ritsuko Akagi, Technological Development Section.

289
00:14:55,680 --> 00:14:56,400
Here's my ID.

290
00:14:56,400 --> 00:15:02,020
I came to see how the new Command Center installation was coming along, but I got lost.

291
00:15:03,180 --> 00:15:06,300
The Commander and Dr. Akagi will see you in the Command Center.

292
00:15:08,380 --> 00:15:09,620
Are you all right?

293
00:15:10,660 --> 00:15:11,180
Yes.

294
00:15:11,360 --> 00:15:13,200
I have no regrets concerning my work.

295
00:15:13,200 --> 00:15:14,200
You're lying.

296
00:15:14,720 --> 00:15:16,660
You still can't forget about Yui, can you?

297
00:15:18,240 --> 00:15:20,520
But that's acceptable to me.

298
00:15:35,480 --> 00:15:37,560
And this is Gehearn headquarters.

299
00:15:39,880 --> 00:15:41,260
Good morning, Commander.

300
00:15:41,260 --> 00:15:43,300
Did you bring your child today?

301
00:15:43,840 --> 00:15:44,220
Oh, wait.

302
00:15:44,320 --> 00:15:46,120
I could have sworn that you had a son.

303
00:15:46,540 --> 00:15:46,940
Oh, no.

304
00:15:47,040 --> 00:15:47,840
This isn't Shinji.

305
00:15:48,140 --> 00:15:50,420
I've decided to take care of an acquaintance's child.

306
00:15:50,860 --> 00:15:52,160
Her name is Rei Ayanami.

307
00:15:52,780 --> 00:15:53,600
Hello, Rei.

308
00:15:53,820 --> 00:15:54,560
I'm Ritsuko.

309
00:15:55,780 --> 00:15:57,800
She resembles someone.

310
00:15:59,460 --> 00:15:59,780
Yui.

311
00:16:02,600 --> 00:16:05,720
All of the records containing Rei Ayanami have been deleted.

312
00:16:06,200 --> 00:16:07,120
They're all blank.

313
00:16:07,220 --> 00:16:08,060
What's going on?

314
00:16:08,060 --> 00:16:11,680
Magi Caspar.

315
00:16:12,420 --> 00:16:13,460
Magi Balthazar.

316
00:16:14,100 --> 00:16:15,020
Magi Melchior.

317
00:16:15,920 --> 00:16:18,100
The Magi are the three aspects of myself.

318
00:16:18,800 --> 00:16:19,900
Myself as a scientist.

319
00:16:20,480 --> 00:16:21,380
Myself as a mother.

320
00:16:21,520 --> 00:16:22,480
And myself as a woman.

321
00:16:22,940 --> 00:16:25,360
The three aspects that combine to make one whole.

322
00:16:25,580 --> 00:16:27,140
The three faces of mother.

323
00:16:27,680 --> 00:16:29,880
And all that's left to do is to turn the power on.

324
00:16:30,260 --> 00:16:30,740
Mm-hmm.

325
00:16:30,740 --> 00:16:33,940
I'll be leaving early today.

326
00:16:34,480 --> 00:16:35,620
Misato just got back.

327
00:16:35,880 --> 00:16:36,460
Oh, yes.

328
00:16:36,880 --> 00:16:38,600
I'd heard that she just joined Gehörn.

329
00:16:38,920 --> 00:16:40,240
In Germany, if I recall.

330
00:16:40,640 --> 00:16:40,980
Yes.

331
00:16:41,220 --> 00:16:42,380
She's with the third branch.

332
00:16:42,560 --> 00:16:44,760
So, she's having a long-distance relationship.

333
00:16:44,960 --> 00:16:46,080
It didn't work out.

334
00:16:46,220 --> 00:16:47,000
They broke up?

335
00:16:47,260 --> 00:16:49,120
But they always seemed like such a perfect couple.

336
00:16:49,120 --> 00:16:52,880
The interaction of men and women isn't very logical.

337
00:16:53,060 --> 00:16:56,160
You're always so cool and analytical about these things.

338
00:16:56,580 --> 00:16:58,740
Aren't you afraid you'll lose your chance at happiness?

339
00:16:59,360 --> 00:17:02,060
First, I have to find a definition of happiness.

340
00:17:03,080 --> 00:17:05,340
It's been a while since I went out.

341
00:17:05,880 --> 00:17:07,040
Well, have a good one.

342
00:17:07,600 --> 00:17:08,280
See you later.

343
00:17:08,280 --> 00:17:23,840
Did you need me for something, Ray?

344
00:17:24,000 --> 00:17:25,500
I lost my way, Doctor.

345
00:17:25,760 --> 00:17:26,680
Is that so?

346
00:17:27,100 --> 00:17:29,020
Well, do you want to come with me, then?

347
00:17:30,480 --> 00:17:31,320
No, thanks.

348
00:17:31,540 --> 00:17:33,380
But how will you get home all by yourself?

349
00:17:34,060 --> 00:17:36,300
That's not your business, old hag.

350
00:17:36,300 --> 00:17:38,500
Old hag?

351
00:17:38,700 --> 00:17:41,500
I can find my way home by myself, old hag.

352
00:17:42,380 --> 00:17:45,220
You shouldn't call someone an old hag, Ray.

353
00:17:45,280 --> 00:17:46,900
But you are an old hag, aren't you?

354
00:17:47,260 --> 00:17:48,420
I'm getting mad.

355
